   "plaque": "arts_druid_theatre",
   "theme": "arts",
   "title": "Druid",
   "text": "Druid was founded in Galway in 1975 by the director Garry Hynes and the actors Marie Mullen and Mick Lally, the first professional theatre company in Ireland outside Dublin. In 1998 Hynes became the first woman to win a Tony Award for directing, for Martin McDonagh's The Beauty Queen of Leenane. In 2005 DruidSynge staged all six of J. M. Synge's plays in a single day, then toured them to the Aran Islands and New York. The tech rehearsal is still going on. It always is."
  }
